{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Fin","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.decay_carried_by_single_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.decay_carried_by_single_block","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L210-L228","doc":"**(CAPSTONE) Under convention D the decay element is carried by a SINGLE\none-dimensional block.**\n\nCombining the two halves: `χ^(2,1)(Δ_S) = 0` kills the 2-dimensional block for\n*every* Markov parameter, and `y_(1³)(z_D) = 0` kills the 3-row block at `z_D`.\nWhat remains is one term. The trace of the decay element at `z_D` is therefore\n`y_(3)(z_D) · χ^(3)(Δ_S)` — one weight, one character.\n\nThe consequence recorded in `qou-cds1`: block re-weighting cannot source the\nconvention-D correction, because after the cap there is only one weight left and\nit is fixed by the trace axioms. An anchor can rescale it and nothing more. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.norm_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.norm_zD","kind":"theorem","line":200,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L200-L206","doc":"**Normalisation `Σ_λ dim_λ y_λ = 1` at `z_D`**, with dimensions `(1,2,1)`\nand the 3-row weight already zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y21_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y21_zD","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L187-L198","doc":"**`y_(2,1)` at `z_D` is `q²/(q²+1)²`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y3_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y3_zD","kind":"theorem","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L170-L185","doc":"**`y_(3)` at `z_D` is `(q⁴+1)/(q²+1)²`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y111_zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y111_zD","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L164-L168","doc":"**The two-row cap: the 3-row block is annihilated at `z_D`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y21","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L154-L156","doc":"The `(2,1)` Ocneanu weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y3","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L149-L152","doc":"The `(3)` Ocneanu weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.y111","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L144-L147","doc":"The `(1³)` Ocneanu weight as a function of `q` and the Markov parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.zD","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L141-L142","doc":"The convention-D Markov parameter `z_D = q³/(q²+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi21_deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi21_deltaS","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L123-L135","doc":"**THE RESULT: the 2-dimensional block does not carry the decay element.**\n`χ^(2,1)(Δ_S) = 0`, exactly, for every `q ≠ 0` and every split `a`. It follows\nfrom the two preceding facts alone — the regular trace vanishes and the two\n1-dimensional characters cancel — so it holds independently of the Markov\nparameter `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.regChar_deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.regChar_deltaS","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L116-L121","doc":"**`Δ_S` is traceless in the regular representation.**\n`reg(Δ_S) = 6·(h²/2) + 3h·a + 3h·(−h−a) = 3h² − 3h² = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi3_add_chi111_deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi3_add_chi111_deltaS","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L107-L114","doc":"**The two 1-dimensional blocks see exactly opposite values.**\n`χ^(3)(Δ_S) + χ^(1³)(Δ_S) = 0`, because `h·(q − q⁻¹) = h²`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi111_deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi111_deltaS","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L101-L105","doc":"**The sign block sees `h²/2 + h·q⁻¹`, independent of the split `a`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi3_deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi3_deltaS","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L95-L99","doc":"**The trivial block sees `h²/2 − h·q`, independent of the split `a`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.deltaS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.deltaS","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L86-L88","doc":"The decay element `Δ_S`, with the `σ₀`/`σ₁` split left free as `a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi21","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi21","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L82-L84","doc":"`χ^(2,1)` as the complement forced by `reg = χ^(3) + 2·χ^(2,1) + χ^(1³)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.regChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.regChar","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L79-L80","doc":"The regular character, extended linearly from `regVal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.regVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.regVal","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L72-L77","doc":"Regular-character values on the NF basis. DATA, from the trace of left\nmultiplication (see the module docstring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi111","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi111","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L69-L70","doc":"`χ^(1³)`, the sign block: `T_w ↦ (−q⁻¹)^len w`, extended linearly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.chi3","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L66-L67","doc":"`χ^(3)`, the trivial block: `T_w ↦ q^len w`, extended linearly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.nfLen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.nfLen","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L63-L64","doc":"Word lengths of the H₃ normal-form basis `[γ, σ₀, σ₁, L₊, L₋, e⁻]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.DecayBlockCarrier.hq","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/DecayBlockCarrier.lean#L60-L61","doc":"`h = q − q⁻¹`, the Hecke parameter. ","signatureChunk":0}]}